    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against soft-throwing rotations. Our premier start is **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), who benefits from a combination of a favorable park factor and a juicy matchup against Mitch Keller. Similarly, **James Wood** (74.59) provides elite value; his presence at the top of the lineup, combined with a 0.407 xwOBA, makes him a primary catalyst for our run production today. **Seiya Suzuki** (67.59) and **Brice Turang** (65.15) round out our strongest plays, with **Brice Turang** specifically boosted by a slow opposing delivery that screams potential for a stolen base\u2014our most critical scarcity category. **Austin Riley** (65.02) also finds a strong floor today against Houser, as the matchup dynamics align to favor his power profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Alex Freeland** (38.92), who fell just shy of our 40-point floor threshold. While his switch-hitting versatility is valuable, the negative variance introduced by a tough matchup against Rasmussen pushed his score into the red zone. We are also managing the absence of **Josh Naylor** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (IL), which thins our bench utility as we continue to lean on **Henry Bolte** (54.23) and **Corbin Carroll** (52.85) to fill our outfield gaps. **Corbin Carroll** presents the most notable risk today, as a high-skill matchup against Detmers suppresses his score, despite his inherent speed threat. We will be monitoring the lineup status of **Cole Young**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Jose Caballero**, who are all hovering near the marginal 50-point mark; if their real-world lineup position drops, we may see them flirt with the \"below floor\" category by game time.",
